    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12469959/comment/12891414",
          "id": "12891414",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=michaelbusch",
            "name": "michaelbusch",
            "key": "michaelbusch",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Busch",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "What shall we do about index backward-compatibility?\n\nI guess 4.0 has to be able to read shared doc stores?  So a lot of that code we can't remove? :(",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=michaelbusch",
            "name": "michaelbusch",
            "key": "michaelbusch",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Busch",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2010-07-23T00:10:33.021+0000",
          "updated": "2010-07-23T00:10:33.021+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12469959/comment/12891422",
          "id": "12891422",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jasonrutherglen",
            "name": "jasonrutherglen",
            "key": "jasonrutherglen",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jason Rutherglen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Maybe we should break backwards-compatibility for the RT branch?  Or just ship an RT specific JAR to keep things simple?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jasonrutherglen",
            "name": "jasonrutherglen",
            "key": "jasonrutherglen",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jason Rutherglen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2010-07-23T00:33:07.181+0000",
          "updated": "2010-07-23T00:33:07.181+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12469959/comment/12891433",
          "id": "12891433",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "The reading side of shared doc stores is quite trivial; I think we should keep it (keep back compat).",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2010-07-23T00:51:47.438+0000",
          "updated": "2010-07-23T00:51:47.438+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12469959/comment/12891558",
          "id": "12891558",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "What are the performance implications of removing shared doc stores? From what I understand, if several segments share the same doc store, then when they are merged, the doc stores aren't merged. Which is a great benefit, especially if you intend to store large fields.\n\nI understand (mostly from the discussion on the PTDW) that with the move to a per-thread approach, the doc stores cannot be shared between segments created by different threads, but what about segments created by the same thread? Are we losing that functionality?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
